# Viaduct — AI Agent Architecture & Guidelines

This file is the definitive reference for AI agents (Cline, Gemini, etc.) and human contributors working on **viaduct**. Project-scoped rules here **override** anything in `/home/bdkl/.clinerules` for work inside this repo.

Before you touch code, read `README.md`, `spec.md`, `roadmap.md`, and `patchnotes.md`. They carry invariants this file does not repeat.

---

## 1. What viaduct Is

**viaduct is a port of NetNewsWire to GTK4 and Rust. That is the entire project.**

NetNewsWire is open-source, battle-tested, and has already solved every hard problem in this domain — feed parsing, date parsing, conditional GETs, article deduplication, coalesced UI updates, memory discipline. We are translating that solution from Swift/AppKit to Rust/GTK4 so Linux users can have it. **We are not designing a new RSS reader.** We are not re-litigating its architectural choices. We port first, then we make it work on Linux.

If you catch yourself thinking "I have a better idea" — you don't. Go read the corresponding Swift file in `.netnewswire/` and port *that*. The app is local-first (local accounts plus Inoreader, and no other remote per §7.3), renders articles through exactly one locked-down `WebKitWebView` (§7.4), and holds to a strict memory budget. Targets GTK4 4.16+ on Wayland (Hyprland or GNOME). **libadwaita was dropped in v3.0.0** (Phase 20); the app is plain GTK4 + WebKitGTK with a viaduct-owned design layer.

Current version: **v3.0.0**. Tagged stable points: v1.6.0 (collects the v1.5.x stability arc — workspace split, Meson, NNW-parity audit, visual identity, theme-contrast picker, adaptive-layout fixes, working YouTube playback via iframe wrapper). The v1.7.x series filled in the obvious missing UI (Add Feed dialog, right-click context menus on sidebar + timeline). v1.8.0 added sync-on-open + periodic-refresh preferences and the written background-daemon plan in `docs/background-service-plan.md`. v1.9.x is the perf-instrumentation arc — `viaduct::perf` log target with structured timing on every sidebar click, cancel-stale-fetch generation counter, bulk folder-aggregation DB op, and the v1.9.1 caps on `strip_html_for_preview` (400 chars) and `scan_html_for_video` (8 KB) that cured the "Digital Antiquarian feels slow" report. **v1.10.0 landed the Phase 17 background daemon**: window-hide-on-close + `run-in-background` GSetting + portal request via `ashpd` + D-Bus re-summon + idle-memory drop on hide. Phase 17's only remaining bullet is the Flathub tag (blocked on user — onboarding credentials, not code). **v2.0.0 ships the Phase 18 architectural refinement**: the three-pane decomposition (`ArticlePaneView` / `TimelineView` / `SidebarView` — pre1/pre2/pre3) shrank `window.rs` from 2900 to 2043 lines (−30 %); pre4 promoted `article_renderer.rs` into a dedicated `ViaductArticleRenderer` GObject with a per-renderer `WebContext` so the `viaduct-img://` + `viaduct-font://` scheme handlers no longer leak onto `WebContext::default()` (and into the video-dialog WebView); pre5 moved unread-count aggregation into `TreeNode` (folder/group totals auto-derive from leaves via `notify::unread-count` cascade); pre6 polished the WebKit ↔ GTK CSS bridge with `currentColor`-driven scrollbars, a 150 ms article-to-article fade-in, and `--accent-color` propagation that picks up the libadwaita system accent for the Adwaita theme. See `roadmap.md` for the live phase plan, `patchnotes.md` for the shipped log, and `docs/debugging.md` for the perf-log workflow.

**License:** MIT. **Edition:** Rust 2024.

---

## 2. Source of Truth: `.netnewswire/`

A full clone of NetNewsWire lives at `.netnewswire/` in this repo. **It is already there — do not re-clone, re-download, or `git submodule add` it.** Treat it as read-only reference material.

> **Note on Latest Upstream Sync (July 17, 2026):**
> The `.netnewswire` reference folder has been fast-forwarded to `08d10f501` (+85 commits over the prior `4c85c907f` sync; the `mac-7.1bN` / `iOS-7.1` beta line). The bulk is out of scope: Mac timeline manual-layout and star-image perf work, appcasts, release notes, CloudKit error strings, SF Symbols. `DateParser`, `OPML`, and the JSON parsers are untouched. The changes that actually reach our derived logic, all ported in **v2.8.3**:
> *   **`ReaderAPIAccountDelegate`: a failed status send must not abort the refresh** (`08d10f501`, `try? await sendArticleStatus()`, fixing [no-feed-updates](https://discourse.netnewswire.com/t/no-feed-updates/336)). We had the same bug and worse: `delegate.rs` used `?` on all four `update_state_to_entries` calls, so one transient failure skipped the status pull *and* the article fetch, and the account silently stopped updating. Ported as a log-and-continue loop. Divergence worth knowing: our `syncStatus` deletes by `articleID` alone (see the grain comment in `sync.rs`), so we clear only articles whose every batch landed; a half-sent article would otherwise lose the row for its other key.
> *   **`ReaderAPICaller.withWriteToken`** (`08134a8fc`): refetch the edit token and retry once on 401/403. Ported as `with_write_token` in `inoreader.rs`, wrapping all seven token-bearing calls (the same seven NNW wraps, `retrieve_entries` included). Ours takes a synchronous builder closure rather than an async operation, because the token only shapes the request body.
> *   **`DownloadSession`: default `Retry-After` of 10 minutes** for 429s that omit the header (`c9bd65b1f`, Reddit). Ported as `DEFAULT_RETRY_AFTER_SECS` + `retry_after_secs` in `fetcher.rs`; our `&&`-chain previously short-circuited and recorded *no* cooldown. The same commit fixes an inverted host filter in `cancelAndRemoveTasksWithHost`; we have no in-flight cancel (cooldowns gate only future `fetch` calls), so nothing to port, but match the corrected semantics if that ever lands.
> *   **`RSCore.StripHTML`: track quoted attribute values** (`d44b3b921`, fixes #5339) so a `>` inside `<source media="(width >= 700px)">` is not read as the tag's end. Ported into `strip_html_for_preview` (`timeline.rs`); ours is char-based and has no script/style tracking, so the quote state is the whole port.
> *   **`XMLEntities`: decode `&zwj;` / `&zwnj;`** (`3a948b755`). We have no entity table (we delegate to `quick_xml`), so this landed as the `escape-html` feature on quick-xml. **That fixed a far worse bug of our own**: without it `unescape()` errors on every named HTML entity, and the parsers' `let Ok(text) = e.unescape() else { continue }` *dropped the text*, so an item titled `Tom &mdash; Jerry` parsed to no title at all. Regression-tested in `parser/xml.rs`.
> *   **Skipped:** `ArticlesTable` (`903e57cfc` de-indent; `5513a7d0e` fixes a `GROUP_CONCAT` authors query written against a schema we never had, since our FTS5 `search` indexes only `title, content_text`); `Author.swift` (comment); `UnreadFeed` (AppDelegate refactor); `WebViewConfiguration` (WKWebView UA); `main.js` `wrapFrames` (our CSP disables JS, so it is dead code for us); `removeLocationHrefRedirectScripts` (`ammonia` strips scripts wholesale).
> *   **Roadmap candidates (recorded in `roadmap.md`):** the Reddit one-feed-per-minute throttle; the `ArticleStringFormatter.sanitizedTitle` port; `core.css`'s `scrollbar-gutter: stable`; feed-declared icon URLs plus the ignore list; icon-background luminance.
>
> **Companion clones:** `.newsflash` and `.liferea` were not re-reviewed this window.
>
> **Note on Prior Upstream Sync (June 20, 2026):**
> The `.netnewswire` reference folder was fast-forwarded to `4c85c907f` (+267 commits over the prior `8c02fb3ba` sync; post-7.0.6, the `mac-7.1bN` beta line). The overwhelming bulk of those commits is a sweeping Swift-concurrency migration (completion-handler to `async`/`await` plus actors) across `Modules/`, alongside CloudKit / Feedbin / Feedly / NewsBlur / ReaderAPI churn (all out of scope per §4). Those mechanical async conversions do not port (we are already async in Rust). Structural-but-inert moves: the 8 `.nnwtheme` bundles relocated from `Shared/Resources/` to a top-level `Themes/` dir (pure rename, zero content change, our bundled copies stay current), and favicon / image / ColorHash code plus `HTMLMetadata` moved into new shared `Modules/Images/` + `Modules/HTMLMetadata/` modules (relocation, not logic change). The changes that actually touch our derived logic:
> *   **`RSParser`: zero changes** this window. Our `parser/` (xml/json/html/date) is fully in sync.
> *   **`ArticlesDatabase`**: no schema change; the article diff (new/updated/deleted), status-row preservation, 6-month-stale rule, and unread-count queries are unchanged in substance. New aggregate helpers (`ArticleCounts` single-query counts, `fetchLastUpdateDates`) are UI-feature-driven; roadmap candidates, not ports.
> *   **`SpecialCases.urlStringMatchesDomain` now matches subdomains** (`host == domain || host.hasSuffix("." + domain)`, plus an empty-domain skip). **Ported in v2.8.2**: `url_host_matches_domain` in `fetcher.rs` accepts exact OR `.`-suffix; the old `..._does_not_match_subdomains` test was inverted to `..._matches_subdomains`. Still safe against the substring attack (`evilrachelbythebay.com`, `rachelbythebay.com.evil.com` rejected).
> *   **`FeedSettings.lastResponseCode` (new `INTEGER` column)** stores the HTTP status of the last download. **Ported in v2.8.2** as `FeedSettings.last_response_code: Option<i64>` (schema column + idempotent ALTER in `settings.rs`; populated in `refresh_one_feed` from `result.status` so 304 / non-200 / success all persist it; the network-error branch leaves the prior value, matching NNW).
> *   **`FeedSettingsDatabase.vacuumIfNeeded(daysBetweenVacuums:)`** throttles VACUUM to once per N days via a new `RSDatabaseInfoTable` key/value table. NNW also switched its DBs to `journal_mode = DELETE` (single-connection rationale); **we keep WAL** (the v2.8.0 read pool needs it), so the journal-mode change is declined. The throttle is **ported in v2.8.2 as a non-regressing hybrid**: a `db_info` table on the articles DB stamps `last_vacuum_date`, and `cleanup_at_startup` now vacuums only when rows were pruned (our v2.8.0 gate) AND `>= VACUUM_INTERVAL_DAYS` (13) have passed. A literal port would have vacuumed every 13 days regardless of pruning, which is more often than our prune gate on a steady-state DB.
> *   **Skipped / roadmap (recorded in `roadmap.md`):** persistent favicon failure caching (transient vs permanent + backoff) and SVG-favicon filtering; the `HTMLMetadata` SQLite cache (slow-network perf); activity-log instrumentation parity (didReceiveResponse / redirect tracking / detailed skip reasons; `FindStrategy` in feed discovery); system suspend/resume timer pause (logind D-Bus); idle-backoff status-sync timer (relevant once Inoreader sync lands).
>
> **Companion `.newsflash` main is unchanged** (`4197c3b3`); active development moved to a `stable` branch plus a new `v.5.1.0` tag. **`.liferea` advanced to `fe797c3`** (comparison only, not a porting source). FeedFinder's logic was unchanged this window (only activity-log instrumentation), so our `feed_discovery.rs` stays current.

> **Note on Prior Upstream Sync (May 27, 2026):**
> The `.netnewswire` reference folder has been fast-forwarded to `8c02fb3ba` (post-7.0.6 App Store release; +99 commits over the prior `4d594181f` sync). The bulk of those commits are iOS/Mac crash fixes, AppleScript additions, appcast/entitlement plumbing, and a new SwiftLint-on-CI setup (they now treat warnings as errors on first-party targets, which we already match with `clippy -D warnings`). The changes that actually touch our `Modules/`-derived logic:
> *   **Parser: skip namespaced subtrees inside an item/entry (Fixes #4422, RSS + Atom).** When parsing is inside an `<item>`/`<entry>`, a namespaced child element (e.g. Shopify's `<s:variant>`) and its *entire subtree* are now skipped via a `namespaceElementDepth` counter, so a nested unprefixed `<title>` ("Default Title") can't be mistaken for the item's own title. **Our `xml.rs` is vulnerable to the same bug**: it tracks only `in_item`, not nested-namespace depth, so an unprefixed element inside a namespaced child is read as the item's. Portable, but note the exclusion set: NNW excludes only `dc:`/`content:`/`source:` from the skip, whereas we additionally consume `media:content`/`media:thumbnail`/`content:encoded`, so our depth-skip must keep those namespaces live. New test fixtures `shopify-namespace.rss` + `draw-down.atom` come with the commit. Roadmap candidate.
> *   **Refresher: minimum time between feed checks lowered 29 → 9 minutes** (`ad7f98d89`). **Ported in v2.8.1** as the named constant `MINIMUM_TIME_BETWEEN_CHECKS_MINUTES` in `fetcher.rs`.
> *   **Refresher: feeds that send `Cache-Control` are governed solely by Cache-Control** (`fd547da76`), exempt from the minimum-time clamp (the 5-hour `max-age` cap still applies). **Ported in v2.8.1**: an early `return None` when `settings.max_age.is_some()`, after the freshness check and before the minimum-time block. `domainsWithNoMinimumTime` is reframed upstream as a safety net for hosts that may *not* send Cache-Control (no change to our 19-host list).
> *   **`ArticleSorter` rewrite.** Now sorts on `logicalDatePublished` (`datePublished ?? dateModified ?? dateArrived`) with `articleID` as the tiebreaker; group-by-feed groups by `feedID` and orders groups by display name (feedID breaks ties). **Partially ported in v2.8.1**: our `SortOrder` now keys on `COALESCE(date_published, date_modified)` (the first two levels of the logical date), keeping the `rowid` tiebreaker (arrival order, more meaningful than a hash for a local store). Group-by-feed was deliberately not adopted (a new sort *mode* / feature, not a fix).
> *   **Author storage refactor** (new `AuthorCache` + `AuthorsSchemaMigration`, deleted `DatabaseObject`/`RelatedObjectsMap` machinery): a Swift DB-layer cleanup. Our `authorsLookup` cascade + orphan sweep already cover this. No port (same call as the #5232 cleanup last sync).
> *   **`DateParser` "change":** whitespace/alignment only (SwiftLint reflow of the timezone-offset table). No behavior change. No port.
> *   **WebKit re-entrancy crash fix** (`107665fa7`, Mac `DetailWebViewController`): guards against re-entering a load during a load callback. Our GTK lockdown profile + single WebView differ; informational only.
> *   **`core.css` / `newsfoot.js` footnote-popover tweaks:** footnote JS never runs under our CSP (`script-src` absent, JS disabled), so `newsfoot.js` is dead for us; the `core.css` `max-width: 44em` footnote-popover change is marginal. No port.
>
> **Companion reference `.newsflash` was also fast-forwarded (to `4197c3b3`).** It is **not** a porting source (we port from NNW per §4), but as the only other serious GTK4/Rust RSS reader it is worth watching. Notable recent moves: (a) **migrated the sidebar and tag lists from `GtkListView` back to `GtkListBox`** while keeping the `TreeListModel` (#731) — a data point that a mature peer found `ListView` painful for a tree sidebar (we use `ListView`); (b) **notification gating** — don't notify when there are zero *unread* (not just zero new), and withdraw the system notification when the window is activated (maps to our `dispatch_refresh_notification` + Phase 17 re-summon); (c) an add-feed **"scrape full articles" toggle** (#905), i.e. reader-on-by-default per feed (we already store `reader_view_always_enabled`); (d) swipe-between-articles (#173) and category-wide settings (#910). These are inspiration, captured as roadmap candidates, not ports.
>
> **Note on Prior Upstream Sync (April 28, 2026):**
> The `.netnewswire` reference folder was updated to upstream `4d594181f` (post-7.0.5 release). Key changes since the previous sync at `ec06277`:
> *   **Parser refactor:** `MutableItem` renamed to `RSSItem` and shared between RSS and Atom parsers. A single `uniqueIDCalculator` is now shared across feed types. Atom now picks up `<icon>` favicons natively and parses `<summary>` correctly. Pure-rename refactors don't translate to our Rust code; keep porting from the new file names.
> *   **`domainsWithNoMinimumTime` expanded** from a small list to 19 domains in `LocalAccountRefresher.swift`. Our `is_no_minimum_domain` should sync to match — folded into v1.0.6 maintenance.
> *   **Macro template format:** NNW article templates use `[[key]]` (double-bracket), not `{{key}}`. Match exactly so themes drop in byte-perfect.
> *   **Issue #5280 / WebView cache:** NNW reverted a change that aggressively emptied the WebKit cache between renders because it triggered intermittent bugs. Lesson for our Phase 6: don't flush WebKit caches between articles. Our memory-only `WebKitNetworkSession` data store sidesteps this automatically.
> *   **Author/authorsLookup startup cleanup (Fixes #5232):** NNW added an explicit cleanup sweep on account init. Our `articles_ad_lookup` cascade trigger handles this differently — no port needed.
> *   **Date parser simplification & swiftString UTF-8 conversion:** Swift-specific micro-perf, not portable to our `chrono` + `quick-xml` stack.
> *   **CloudKit Storage Stats UI:** out of scope (we don't ship CloudKit).
> *   **Themes unchanged** since previous sync — Phase 6 plan to bundle all 8 (`Sepia`, `Appanoose`, `Biblioteca`, `Hyperlegible`, `NewsFax`, `Promenade`, `Tiqoe Dark`, `Verdana Revival`) is unaffected.

When you need to implement a feature, port from this local tree. Do not invent bespoke logic.

Key paths to consult:

| viaduct target | NetNewsWire source |
|---|---|
| `src/parser/xml.rs`, `src/parser/json.rs`, `src/parser/html.rs` | `.netnewswire/Modules/RSParser/Sources/RSParser/` (see `Feeds/XML/`, `Feeds/JSON/`, `HTML/`) |
| `src/parser/date.rs` (`DateParser` port) | `.netnewswire/Modules/RSParser/Sources/RSParser/Utilities/DateParser.swift` |
| `src/database/articles.rs` | `.netnewswire/Modules/ArticlesDatabase/Sources/ArticlesDatabase/` and `.netnewswire/Modules/Articles/Sources/Articles/` |
| `src/database/settings.rs`, `src/database/opml.rs`, `src/database/accounts.rs` | `.netnewswire/Modules/Account/Sources/Account/` (`FeedSettingsDatabase.swift`, `OPMLFile.swift`, `OPMLNormalizer.swift`, `LocalAccount/LocalAccountDelegate.swift`) |
| `src/network/fetcher.rs` | `.netnewswire/Modules/RSWeb/Sources/RSWeb/` plus `.netnewswire/Modules/Account/Sources/Account/LocalAccount/LocalAccountRefresher.swift` |
| Coalescing / BatchUpdate primitives | `.netnewswire/Modules/RSCore/Sources/RSCore/` (`CoalescingQueue.swift`, `BatchUpdate.swift`) and `.netnewswire/Modules/RSDatabase/Sources/RSDatabase/` (`DatabaseQueue.swift`) |
| Feed discovery from a website URL | `.netnewswire/Modules/FeedFinder/Sources/FeedFinder/` |

`.gitignore` may or may not exclude `.netnewswire/` depending on the branch; in either case, never commit changes inside it.

